<article class="env-lemma" id="0469">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0469">Lemma <span data-tag="0469">73.7.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ be an fppf covering of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then the map of sheaves </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \coprod X_ i \longrightarrow X  \]
</div>
  <p> is surjective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05VM" data-tag="05VM">65.5.9</a>. See also Spaces, Remark <a href="/tag/02YN" data-tag="02YN">65.5.2</a> in case you are confused about the meaning of this lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>